# Agent notes (self-evolve)

`docs/NOTES.md` is the live unresolved scratchpad. Keep it tiny.
Measured objectives/scores live in `PROGRESS.md`, fixed causes in
`DIVERGENCE-LOG.md`, structural omissions in `C-JS-MAP.md`, and loop chronology
in `AGENT-LOOP-JOURNAL.md`.

## What belongs in NOTES.md

- Active hypothesis + one command that would falsify it
- Current expensive dead ends labeled “don’t re-check” with the counterexample
- Session landmarks (e.g. 0-RNG keys at `--More--`; key attribution ≠ RNG order)
- Open questions only — not peel chronology (journal) or resolved causes
  (divergence log)

## What does not

Constitution, strategy essays, resolved peel chronology, baseline scores, and
module status — those have other owners.

## When to write

After any diagnosis that burned a long wrong path, add 3–5 lines to
`docs/NOTES.md` **before** the next peel. Once resolved, move the evidence to
`DIVERGENCE-LOG.md` and remove stale detail from Notes. Prefer falsifying
against session **screens + key/RNG maps** early (not only `rng-diff` call
sites).

## Self-reflect

Update Notes when evidence shows the working theory is wrong. Ordinary loop
porters must not rewrite this rule, the Constitution, or the runbook; propose
process changes in the journal for human/auditor review. Drop the theory—do
not invent alignment machinery to save it.
